@startuml
title RTSyn v1.0.0 - Process and dependency view

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
left to right direction

actor User

package "Client process: rtsyn" {
    component "GUI\nmain thread" as Gui
    component "GUI worker\nHTTP + JSONL reader" as GuiWorker
    component "CLI\nHTTP commands" as Cli
    database "Workspace TOML\nand UI metadata" as Workspace

    Gui --> GuiWorker
    Gui --> Workspace
    Cli --> Workspace
}

cloud "HTTP\n127.0.0.1:17190" as HttpTransport

package "Daemon process: rtsyn --no-gui daemon run" {
    component "HTTP API\nserver thread" as Api
    component "Telemetry drain\nnon-RT thread" as Drain

    queue "Command SPSC\nAPI -> RT" as Commands
    queue "Result SPSC\nRT -> API" as Results
    queue "Telemetry event SPSC\nRT -> drain" as Events
    queue "Telemetry value ring\nRT -> drain" as Values

    component "Engine RT cycle thread\ncommands, runtime step, absolute sleep" as Engine
    component "Engine wait thread\njoin and lifecycle" as Wait
    component "Runtime\ngraph and deterministic stages" as Runtime
}

component "ABI plugin and device nodes" as Nodes
component "Physical hardware\nor external system" as Hardware
database "Telemetry files\nJSONL values and optional CSV" as TelemetryFiles

User --> Gui : default frontend
User --> Cli : --no-gui
GuiWorker --> HttpTransport : HTTP
Cli --> HttpTransport : HTTP
HttpTransport --> Api

Api --> Commands : control request
Commands --> Engine : consume at cycle boundary
Engine --> Results : result / descriptor
Results --> Api : response or snapshot

Engine --> Runtime : one cycle
Runtime --> Nodes : ABI callbacks
Nodes --> Hardware : device read / write
Wait --> Engine : join after stop

Engine --> Events : lifecycle and measurement events
Engine --> Values : subscribed samples
Events --> Drain
Values --> Drain
Drain --> TelemetryFiles : append JSONL / CSV
GuiWorker --> TelemetryFiles : tail live values

note bottom of Runtime
Cycle order: device read, current-cycle propagation, plugin processing,
current-cycle propagation, device write. Only a plugin-to-plugin edge that
closes a cycle is staged for the next cycle.
end note

note bottom of Commands
All four queues are fixed-capacity POSIX shared-memory SPSC channels.
Their hot paths are non-blocking and allocation-free after setup.
end note

note bottom of Gui
GUI and CLI are clients only. Workspaces are client-side and never own
the runtime graph.
end note

@enduml
